{"_id":"68d3f5e9166b018f83df6239","roadmapSlug":"html","nodeId":"GpaI2IDHDOZjyT3AZMbYD","description":"# Style Attribute\n\nThe `style` attribute in HTML allows you to apply CSS (Cascading Style Sheets) directly to individual HTML elements. It's used to define inline styles, overriding external stylesheets or default browser styles. You can set properties like color, font, size, and layout directly within the HTML tag.","resources":[{"type":"article","title":"HTML style global attribute","url":"https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Global_attributes/style","_id":"6a71e295b0650226a59f1b7e"},{"type":"article","title":"HTML style","url":"https://www.codecademy.com/resources/docs/html/attributes/style","_id":"6a71e295b0650226a59f1b7f"},{"type":"video","title":"HTML Style Attribute | Mastering of Web development","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zk97ve9JM6A","_id":"6a71e295b0650226a59f1b80"}],"createdAt":"2025-09-24T13:45:13.913Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-04T13:01:09.024Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a10b41ba95e0d5c68dede2f","title":"HTML Fundamentals","slug":"html","description":"Enough HTML to read, write, inspect, and understand real web pages.","lessonIds":["6a0da437a95e0d5c68ded033","6a0ef00da95e0d5c68ded162","6a0f1366a95e0d5c68ded2b4","6a0f2262a95e0d5c68ded32a","6a0f33e7a95e0d5c68ded463","6a102d2fa95e0d5c68ded758","6a106a2ba95e0d5c68deda00","6a107b29a95e0d5c68deda53"],"projectIds":["68b7185fffbff9183d772aea","68b7185fffbff9183d772aeb","6a1485bfac1c5fa9928a2087","6a1485c5ac1c5fa9928a2093","6a1485cbac1c5fa9928a2099","6a1485d1ac1c5fa9928a20a4"],"featuredImage":"","readingTime":58,"lessonCount":8,"quizCount":0,"projectCount":6}],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/html/content/GpaI2IDHDOZjyT3AZMbYD.md"}